{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:addc562983d9fb4f","name":"Lectroticker","source":{"id":"source:reference-addc562983d9fb4f","title":"Lectroticker","revision":18952,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:01:54Z","sha256":"d879df20e802bdeffc6f701292abbbeca9c7137b0c8662c382a63d08d78ea831","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18952","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Lectroticker&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-addc562983d9fb4f","blocks":[{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["LECTROTICKER\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["COST\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+2\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["1,500\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+4\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["3,000\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["4,500\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["+8\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["6,000\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["etc...\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["etc...\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Cost:"]}," 1,500 per +2 (see right)\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Weight:"]}," 1 Kilogram\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A small electronic device used to bypass low-grade security systems, a Lectroticker consists of several small wires connected to a sense-plate. When the sense-plate is inserted into a standard security lock (such as those found on doors throughout the galaxy), the sense-plate is charged with varying amounts of energy, scrambling the signals sent to the electronic lock, and fooling its systems into thinking that the correct access card has been provided. A Lectroticker can be activated as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Action"},", after which it makes a single ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," check (with a bonus of +2 or higher, determined by its cost and quality) to disable an electric lock. All Lectrotickers are considered ",{"tag":"a","children":["Illegal"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Illegal"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The quality of a Lectroticker  is reflected in its cost, as every +2 bonus to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," checks increases the cost of a Lectroticker by 1,500 credits, as the side-table indicates.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
